<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68249" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόδιος</span></b> , ὁ,
		= Lat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>modius</i>, a dry measure, =
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέδιμνος</span>, for which it is
				f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Din.
				1.43
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				533.30
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>vessel of this capacity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Matt.
				5.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a measure of
			length, =
			<i><span class="en">
				200
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργυιαί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Geom.</i><i><span class="en">
				4.12
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
